@startuml
title Digital Credential Issuance part 2 : wallet receives and stores the credential (SD-JWT VC, HSM-backed Issuer, On-Device Credential Model)

participant User
participant "<color:#white>Mobile App (Core ทางรัฐ)</color>" as CoreApp #2E7D32
participant "<color:#white>Document Wallet (Miniapp)</color>" as Mini #2E7D32
participant "<color:#white>DW Core</color>" as DW #steelblue
participant "<color:#white>VCVP Core</color>" as Core #3F51B5
participant "<color:#white>one-core (Credential Engine)</color>" as Engine #chocolate
participant "<color:#white>HSM</color>" as HSM #darkgoldenrod
participant "<color:#white>Trust Registry ETDA</color>" as Trust #darkviolet

note over Mini,Engine #orange: 7. Wallet Resolves Credential Offer

note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] OpenID4VCI 1.0 section 13.4 Split-Architecture Wallets\nThe app resolves the offer itself , DW Core only passes the OfferUrl and never holds the pre-authorized_code\n(13.4 : a server component with access to pre-authorized codes MAY be able to impersonate the application)\nIssuer trust check is done on the app (design choice , 13.5 requires the Wallet to validate the Credential Issuer)

Mini->Mini: Parse OfferUrl to get credential_offer_uri

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Protocol endpoints (/ssi , /.well-known) carry no Consumer-Key\noffer , token , credential , notification write VCVPAuditLog (Actor Channel = WALLET , no caller OrgCode)\nissuer metadata , authorization server metadata , nonce , DID document , vct type metadata are public reads\nrecorded only in the access log , not in VCVPAuditLog

Mini->Core: Read offer from credential_offer_uri | GET /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/offer/{credentialId} (URL = credential_offer_uri in OfferUrl , {credentialSchemaId} and {credentialId} are engine ids inside it)
Core->Engine: Read offer from credential_offer_uri | GET /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/offer/{credentialId} (VCVP Core 11)
Engine-->Core: credential_issuer , credential_configuration_ids , grants.pre-authorized_code
Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store pre-authorized_code (= engine interaction id) in Documents table EngineRefs[].RefInteractionId\n(document found by {credentialId} in the offer path = EngineRefs[].RefDocumentId)
Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of /ssi offer (EngineCalls , Correlation.DocumentId)
Mini<--Core: credential offer | credential_issuer , credential_configuration_ids , grants.pre-authorized_code
Mini->Mini: Keep pre-authorized_code (for token request in section 8)\nKeep credential_issuer (for issuer metadata URL , proof aud , trust check)\nKeep credential_configuration_ids (for credential type)\nBuild issuer metadata URL = /.well-known/openid-credential-issuer + path of credential_issuer

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Values declared in metadata\nformat = dc+sd-jwt\ncryptographic_binding_methods_supported = [ jwk , did:web , did:tdw , did:key , did:ion , did:jwk ]\njwk is listed , so the holder can bind with a raw public key without a DID\ncredential_signing_alg_values_supported = [ ES256 , EdDSA , ML-DSA-65 ]\nproof_types_supported.jwt supports ES256
Mini->Core: Read issuer metadata from credential_issuer | GET /.well-known/openid-credential-issuer/ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/{identifierId}/{credentialSchemaId} (URL = /.well-known/openid-credential-issuer + path of credential_issuer from the offer , {protocolId} = OPENID4VCI_FINAL1 , {identifierId} = engine id of the issuer identifier , {credentialSchemaId})
Core->Engine: Read issuer metadata from credential_issuer | GET /.well-known/openid-credential-issuer/ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/{identifierId}/{credentialSchemaId} (VCVP Core 12)
Engine-->Core: credential_endpoint , nonce_endpoint , notification_endpoint,credential_configurations_supported
Mini<--Core: issuer metadata | credential_endpoint , nonce_endpoint , notification_endpoint,credential_configurations_supported
note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] OpenID4VCI 1.0 section 12.2.4 : credential_issuer in metadata MUST be identical to the identifier\nused to build the metadata URL , otherwise the metadata MUST NOT be used
Mini->Mini: Check credential_issuer in metadata = credential_issuer from offer\n(simple string comparison)
alt credential_issuer in metadata does not match
    Mini->DW: Report issuance result + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/issuance_result (DW endpoint 06)\n(issuanceSessionId from response of 1.2 , result = FAILED , reason = ISSUER_METADATA_INVALID)
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of issuance_result) | reason = ISSUER_METADATA_INVALID
    Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added , the offer expires by itself , sections 7.1 to 11 do not apply
else Metadata valid
    Mini->Mini: Continue
end
note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] OpenID4VCI 1.0 section 12.2.4 (credential_metadata) : for SD-JWT VC , type metadata of the vct is preferred for display , credential_metadata is the fallback\nEngine vct type metadata uses key instead of technicalKey and lang instead of locale , so the preview uses credential_metadata
Mini->Mini: Keep nonce_endpoint , credential_endpoint , notification_endpoint (for section 8 , 9)\nKeep proof types , signing alg , binding method (for proof JWT in section 8.1)\nKeep issuer display (name , logo) and credential display (name , logo) (for preview)\nKeep claims display (path , display name , mandatory) from credential_configurations_supported.{id}.credential_metadata (for preview)\nAuthorization server = authorization_servers if declared , otherwise credential_issuer

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] Access token is a Bearer token , the wallet does not send DPoP\n(metadata lists dpop_signing_alg_values_supported but the engine does not check it)
Mini->Core: Get authorization server metadata from authorization server | GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/{identifierId}/{credentialSchemaId} (URL = /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server + path of credential_issuer , the metadata declares no authorization_servers)
Core->Engine: Get authorization server metadata from authorization server | GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/{identifierId}/{credentialSchemaId} (VCVP Core 13)
Engine-->Core: token_endpoint\ngrant_types_supported = [ pre-authorized_code , refresh_token ]
Mini<--Core: authorization server metadata | token_endpoint
Mini->Mini: Keep token_endpoint (for token request in section 8)

note over Mini #violet: 7.1 Wallet Reads Issuer Trust Result
note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] issuerTrust is the result of the issuing side check (VCVP Core , section 5) , not a check by the wallet\ncredential_issuer in the offer is an engine URL , it is not an identifier listed in the Trust Registry\nThe wallet checks the issuer DID (iss) against the Trust Registry in section 9\n(OpenID4VCI 1.0 section 13.5 : the Wallet MUST perform validation checks on the Credential Issuer)
Mini->Mini: Read issuerTrust from response of 1.2\n(result of the VCVP Core trust check in section 5)

note over User,Mini #lightblue: 7.2 User Reviews Credential
Mini-->User: Show preview\nissuer (issuer display from metadata) , credential type (credential display from metadata)\nlist of data in the credential (claims display names from metadata , no values)\nissuer trust result (issuerTrust from response of 1.2)

alt Holder accepts credential
    User->Mini: Accept

    note over CoreApp,HSM #orange: 8. Issue Credential

    Mini->Core: Request access token with pre-authorized_code (from offer) | POST token_endpoint (from authorization server metadata) = /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/token
    Core->Engine: Request access token with pre-authorized_code (from offer) | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/token (VCVP Core 14)\npre-authorized code

    alt Pre-authorized code expired / invalid
        Engine-->Core: error
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of /ssi token (FailureReason = PRE_AUTHORIZED_CODE_INVALID , Correlation.DocumentId)
        Mini<--Core: error (offer expired)
        Mini->DW: Request new offer + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/offer_renew (DW endpoint 05)\n(issuanceSessionId from response of 1.2)
        DW->Core: Request new offer link | POST /vcvp/v1/documents/offer (VCVP Core 09) (DocumentId stored in the DW issuance request)
        Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) , caller channel = WALLET , ActorType = CITIZEN\nwrite access log
        Core->Core: Validate caller authorization
        alt Caller not authorized
            Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 09 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED , Correlation.DocumentId)
            DW<--Core: 403 | FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
            DW->DW: Update issuance request status = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
            Mini<--DW: Error (response of offer_renew) | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
            Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
            note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , card/document not added
        else Caller authorized
            Core->Core: Continue to renew offer link
        end
        note right of Engine #wheat:[SPEC] Engine allows share again when state is CREATED , PENDING or INTERACTION_EXPIRED\nAfter the token exchange the state is OFFERED , share is refused (400 BR_0002)\nOFFERED does not change when the offer expires , the holder can still get the credential with its access token\nIn OFFERED state a new credential must be created (section 5 and 6)
        Core->Engine: Get credential state | GET /api/credential/v1/{CREDENTIAL_ID} (VCVP Core 09) (CREDENTIAL_ID from Documents table EngineRefs[].RefDocumentId)
        Engine-->Core: state

        alt State CREATED / PENDING / INTERACTION_EXPIRED
            Core->Engine: Create offer link | POST /api/credential/v1/{CREDENTIAL_ID}/share (VCVP Core 09) (CREDENTIAL_ID from Documents table EngineRefs[].RefDocumentId)
            Engine-->Core: url = openid-credential-offer://?credential_offer_uri=...\nexpiresAt
            Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store new offer in Documents table (OfferUrl , OfferExpiresAt , Status = PENDING)
            Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 09 (renew , EngineCalls , Correlation.DocumentId)
            DW<--Core: 200 | DocumentId + OfferUrl + ExpiresAt
        else State OFFERED
            Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 09 (FailureReason = OFFER_NOT_RENEWABLE , EngineCalls , Correlation.DocumentId)
            DW<--Core: 409 | FailureReason = OFFER_NOT_RENEWABLE
            DW->DW: Repeat section 5 and 6 (VCVP Core 08)\nto create a new document and offer
        end

        DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store new DocumentId + OfferUrl + ExpiresAt in DW database (issuance request)\n+ new IssuerTrust when section 5 and 6 ran again (state OFFERED)
        Mini<--DW: 200 (response of offer_renew) | new OfferUrl + ExpiresAt
        Mini->Mini: Repeat section 7 with the new OfferUrl
        Mini->Mini: Repeat section 8 from the access token request
    else Access token issued
        Engine->Engine: State PENDING → OFFERED
        Engine-->Core: access token
        Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of /ssi token (Correlation.DocumentId)
        Mini<--Core: access token
    end

    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] OpenID for Verifiable Credential Issuance 1.0 (OpenID4VCI 1.0 Final , Sep 2025) section 7 Nonce Endpoint\nThe engine has only OpenID4VCI 1.0 Final installed (protocol OPENID4VCI_FINAL1) , so there is no choice to make here\nNonce is fetched once and used for every proof in the same batch
    Mini->Core: Request nonce | POST nonce_endpoint (from issuer metadata) = /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/nonce
    Core->Engine: Request nonce | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{protocolId}/nonce (VCVP Core 15)
    Engine-->Core: c_nonce
    Mini<--Core: c_nonce

    note over CoreApp #f4cccc: 8.1 Holder Proof of Possession (signing point 1)

    Mini->CoreApp: Build and sign proof JWT (c_nonce , credential_issuer from the offer as aud)
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] proof header must contain exactly one of kid or jwk\nnot both and not neither\nThe schema sets KeyStorageSecurity , so the header is kid = index of the key in the key attestation ("0") + key_attestation (WUA) , without jwk\nthe engine then takes the holder public key from the attestation\niss must be omitted because a pre-authorized code is used (OpenID4VCI)\nNormally one signature , with batch enabled one proof per key , all sent together
    CoreApp->CoreApp: Load key attestation (WUA) of the holder key (from section 1.2)
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] No wallet unit or key attestation on this device : register and activate the wallet unit as in section 1.2 first
    alt Key attestation expired (valid 31 days)
        CoreApp->Core: Request key attestation | POST /ssi/wallet-unit/v1/{id}/issue-attestation\n(wua : proof signed with the holder key , security_level)
        Core->Engine: Request key attestation | POST /ssi/wallet-unit/v1/{id}/issue-attestation
        Engine-->Core: WUA (key-attestation+jwt)
        CoreApp<--Core: WUA
        CoreApp->CoreApp: [DATA STORE] Store new WUA with the holder key
    else Key attestation valid
        CoreApp->CoreApp: Continue
    end
    loop Repeat per holder key
        CoreApp->CoreApp: Load holder private key (created and registered in section 1.2)\nSecure Enclave (iOS) / Android Keystore / StrongBox
        CoreApp->CoreApp: Build proof JWT and sign with on-device key\ntyp = openid4vci-proof+jwt , alg = ES256\nkid = "0" , key_attestation = WUA (no jwk) , aud = credential_issuer (from offer) , nonce = c_nonce , iat
    end
CoreApp-->Mini: proof JWT (one per holder key)

    Mini->Core: Request credential with access token + proof JWT | POST credential_endpoint (from issuer metadata) = /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/credential\ncredential_configuration_id (from offer) , proofs = { jwt : [ proof JWT ] }
    note over Core,Engine #orange: 8.2 Verify Holder Proof
    note right of Core #wheat:[ENGINE RULE] The engine checks the key attestation signature with the key in the attestation header\nit does not check who issued the attestation , an attestation signed by the wallet itself is accepted
    Core->Core: Check the key attestation in the proof header is signed by a trusted wallet provider\n(wallet provider list kept by VCVP Core)
    alt Key attestation not signed by a trusted wallet provider
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of /ssi credential (FailureReason = KEY_ATTESTATION_FAILED , Correlation.DocumentId)
        Mini<--Core: Reject with reason (invalid_proof)
        Mini->DW: Report issuance result + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/issuance_result (DW endpoint 06)\n(issuanceSessionId from response of 1.2 , result = FAILED , reason = KEY_ATTESTATION_FAILED)
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of issuance_result) | reason = KEY_ATTESTATION_FAILED
        Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
        note over User,Mini #wheat: VC not stored , card/document not added
    else Trusted wallet provider
        Core->Core: Continue
    end
    Core->Engine: Request credential with access token + proof JWT | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/credential (VCVP Core 16)\naccess token + all proof JWTs

    Engine->Engine: Check typ is openid4vci-proof+jwt
    Engine->Engine: Check exactly one of kid or jwk , extract holder public key
    Engine->Engine: Verify proof signature with that public key
    Engine->Engine: Check nonce matches and is unused , and aud is this issuer
    Engine->Engine: Check key attestation : key_storage contains the level set on the schema (KeyStorageSecurity)\nsignature with the key in the attestation header , not expired , not revoked

    alt Proof invalid / offer expired / already used
        Engine-->Core: error
        Core->Core: Update status = ISSUANCE_FAILED
        note right of Core #wheat:[ERROR AUDIT] VCVPAuditLog\nFailureReason = INVALID_PROOF / OFFER_EXPIRED / OFFER_ALREADY_USED / KEY_ATTESTATION_FAILED\nMessageCode , Message (HTTP status of the error)\nEngineCalls[].ErrorCode , EngineCalls[].ErrorMessage (engine error)\nEngineCalls[].RefEntityId (engine credential id)\nCorrelation.DocumentId\nEventTime\nActor (Channel = WALLET)\nCorrelation.RequestId
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of /ssi credential\n(FailureReason = INVALID_PROOF / OFFER_EXPIRED / OFFER_ALREADY_USED / KEY_ATTESTATION_FAILED , Correlation.DocumentId)

        Mini<--Core: Reject with reason
        Mini->DW: Report issuance result + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/issuance_result (DW endpoint 06)\n(issuanceSessionId from response of 1.2 , result = FAILED , reason)
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of issuance_result) | reason = ISSUANCE_FAILED
        Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
        note over User,Mini #wheat: VC not stored , card/document not added
    else Proof valid

        note over Engine,HSM #f4cccc: 8.3 Issuer Signs the Credential (signing point 2)

        Engine->Engine: Reserve an index in the Token Status List\nget { uri , idx } and embed it as status in the token
        Engine->Engine: Embed holder public key from the proof as cnf
        Engine->Engine: Build SD_JWT_VC and compute _sd digests of selectively disclosable claims

        note right of Engine #wheat:[SIGNING POINT 2] Signed token structure\nheader : typ = dc+sd-jwt , alg = ES256\nkid = verificationMethod id of the issuer did:web , format did:web:...#key-{keyId}\npayload : vct , vct#integrity , iss = issuer did:web\niat , nbf , status.status_list = { uri , idx } (Token Status List)\ncnf.jwk = holder public key , raw EC P-256\n_sd = digests , _sd_alg = sha-256\nDisclosures appended with ~ , each is [ salt , technicalKey , value ]\n\nsub is present only when the holder uses a DID identifier\nWith a KEY identifier , as chosen , there is no sub and no holder DID anywhere in the credential\nexp is present only when credential validity is configured , otherwise only iat and nbf
        note right of Engine #wheat:[SIGNING POINT 2] Required setup , otherwise signing fails\n1. The issuing key must be declared in the DID Document under assertionMethod\nthe engine looks up kid in this relationship , signing fails if not found\n2. The vct URL must be resolvable , by default the engine hosts it at /ssi/vct/v2/{orgId}/{schemaId}/SD_JWT_VC\nif moved to our domain it must still resolve\n3. The Token Status List must be published and resolvable at /ssi/revocation/v1/list/{id}\nthe list is a JWT signed with the same issuer key
        Engine->HSM: Sign SD-JWT (JWS) with issuer signing key (ECDSA / ES256)
        HSM-->Engine: Issuer signature

        Engine->Engine: State OFFERED → ACCEPTED
        Engine-->Core: SD_JWT_VC (signed) + all disclosures + notification_id
        Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Update Documents : Status = ACTIVE and EngineRefs[].RefNotificationId = notification_id\n(document found by the access token , the part before the dot = engine interaction id = EngineRefs[].RefInteractionId)

        note over Core #lightgreen: 8.4 Issuance Audit Log
        note right of Core #wheat:[AUDIT LOG] VCVPAuditLog\nEventType = DOCUMENT_ACCEPTED\nEngineCalls[].RefEntityId (engine credential id)\nCorrelation.DocumentId\nEventTime\nIntegrity.Hash , Integrity.PrevHash\nno personal data claims in the audit trail
        Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of /ssi credential (EngineCalls , Correlation.DocumentId)

        Mini<--Core: Credential (SD_JWT_VC + all disclosures) + notification_id
        Mini->Mini: Keep notification_id (for notification in section 9)\nRead iss and kid from the credential (for issuer DID document)\nRead vct from the credential (for vct type metadata)

        note over Mini,CoreApp #lightblue: 9. Wallet Verifies Before Storing
        note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] Goal : the app checks the credential is genuine and usable before saving it\nCheck 1 : the issuer really signed it and nothing was changed (see the note above Verify issuer signature)\nCheck 2 : the issuer is trusted (issuer DID (iss) is listed in the Trust Registry and its accreditation has not expired)\nCheck 3 : the credential is bound to this phone (holder key in the credential (cnf.jwk) = the key on this device)\nCheck 4 : the credential type is the one offered and its description was not changed (vct , vct#integrity)\nAny check fails : tell the engine (credential_failure) and DW (issuance_result FAILED) , the card/document is not added\nAll checks pass : save the credential (9.1 , 9.2) , tell the engine (credential_accepted) and DW (issuance_result ACCEPTED) (9.3)
        Mini->Mini: Build the DID document URL from the issuer DID (iss , did:web method)\nremove did:web: , replace : with / , decode %3A , add /did.json\nresult : https://{host}/ssi/did-web/v1/{id}/did.json ({id} = last segment of the issuer DID)
        Mini->Core: Get issuer DID document from the URL built above | GET /ssi/did-web/v1/{id}/did.json
        Core->Engine: Get issuer DID document | GET /ssi/did-web/v1/{id}/did.json (VCVP Core 17)
        Engine-->Core: DID document | verificationMethod[] { id , publicKeyJwk }
        Mini<--Core: DID document | verificationMethod[] { id , publicKeyJwk }
        Mini->CoreApp: Verify the issuer signature of the credential (Check 1) (credential , issuer DID document)
        note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] Goal : prove the credential was signed by the issuer and was not changed\nRequired by RFC 9901 (SD-JWT) section 7.2 , done on the app because only the app receives the full credential\nStep 1 : read from the credential the signing key id (kid) and the issuer (iss)\nStep 2 : check the key belongs to the issuer (the DID before # in kid = iss)\nStep 3 : in the issuer DID document (request above) , find the public key whose id = kid\nStep 4 : check that key is allowed to sign credentials (kid is listed in assertionMethod)\nStep 5 : give the credential and that public key to an SD-JWT library , it checks the signature and every disclosure\nLibrary : eudi-lib-jvm-sdjwt-kt (Android) , eudi-lib-sdjwt-swift (iOS) , sd-jwt-js (JS)\nWith the Procivis wallet SDK , steps 1 to 5 run inside issuance-accept\nAny step fails → Verification failed branch below
        CoreApp->CoreApp: Verify issuer signature (Check 1)\nusing the public key of the verificationMethod matching kid
        CoreApp-->Mini: Check 1 result
        Mini->Trust: Check issuer DID (iss) is listed and accreditation not expired (Check 2) | GET {trust registry URL}
        Trust-->Mini: Accreditation status
        Mini->CoreApp: Check the credential is bound to this device (Check 3) (cnf.jwk in the credential)
        note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] Why the holder key is checked now (Check 3)\nThe credential works only with the key whose public key is in cnf.jwk\nIf that is not the key on this device , the user can never present this credential to a verifier\n(the app cannot create the key binding proof (Key Binding JWT) that the verifier requires)\nCheck it here before saving , not later when the user presents the credential
        CoreApp->CoreApp: Check cnf.jwk matches the public key of the key on this device (Check 3)
        CoreApp-->Mini: Check 3 result
        Mini->Core: Get credential type description from the vct URL in the credential (vct type metadata) | GET /ssi/vct/v2/{orgId}/{credentialSchemaId}/SD_JWT_VC (URL = vct in the credential , {orgId} = engine id of the issuer organisation)
        Core->Engine: Get credential type description (vct type metadata) | GET /ssi/vct/v2/{orgId}/{credentialSchemaId}/SD_JWT_VC (VCVP Core 18)
        Engine-->Core: credential type description (vct type metadata)
        Mini<--Core: credential type description (vct type metadata)
        Mini->Mini: Check the credential type (Check 4)\nvct in the credential = the credential type that was offered (credential_configuration_id)\nhash of the credential type description just downloaded = vct#integrity in the credential

        alt Any check fails (Check 1 to 4)
            note right of Mini #wheat:[SPEC] Failure reason per check (for developers)\nCheck 1 issuer signature invalid : VERIFICATION_FAILED\nCheck 2 issuer not in the Trust Registry or accreditation expired : ISSUER_NOT_TRUSTED\nCheck 3 cnf.jwk is not the key on this device : HOLDER_KEY_MISMATCH\nCheck 4 vct or vct#integrity does not match the offer : CREDENTIAL_TYPE_MISMATCH\nThe reason goes to DW in issuance_result and to VCVP in event_description of the notification (OpenID4VCI 1.0 section 11.1)\nVCVP Core reads event_description before forwarding and stores it in FailureReason , the engine does not keep it
            Mini->DW: Report issuance result + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/issuance_result (DW endpoint 06)\n(issuanceSessionId from response of 1.2 , result = FAILED , reason of the failed check (see note) ,\nnotification_id , access token , notification_endpoint)
            DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUANCE_FAILED\n(VC not issued , card/document not added)
            note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Same two ways as section 9.3 : the app may notify the engine directly ,\nthis flow sends credential_failure through DW
            DW->Core: Notify credential_failure with notification_id + access token | POST notification_endpoint (from issuer metadata , passed by the app) = /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification
            note right of Engine #wheat:[SPEC] OpenID4VCI 1.0 section 11.1 : credential_failure is used for unsuccessful cases not caused by a user action\ncredential_deleted is used only when the user caused it
            Core->Engine: Notify credential_failure with notification_id + access token | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification (VCVP Core 19)\nevent = credential_failure
            Engine->Engine: State ACCEPTED → ERROR
            Engine-->Core: 204
            Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Documents Status = ISSUANCE_FAILED , WalletNotification (Event = credential_failure , ReceivedAt , FailureReason from event_description)\n(document found by notification_id = EngineRefs[].RefNotificationId)
            Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of /ssi notification (FailureReason = reason from event_description , event = credential_failure , Correlation.DocumentId)
            DW<--Core: 204
            Mini<--DW: Error (response of issuance_result) | reason of the failed check
            Mini-->User: Show error , card/document not added (reason)
            note over User,Mini #wheat: VC not stored , card/document not added
        else Verification passed

            note over CoreApp #lightblue: 9.1 Credential Storage Model (on device or cloud)
            note right of CoreApp #wheat:[PENDING] Two storage modes are kept in the design , one will be removed later\nIn both modes the holder private key stays on the device
            Mini->CoreApp: Store the credential (SD_JWT_VC + all disclosures)
            alt Storage mode = ON_DEVICE
                note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] On-device credential model\nThe wallet owns the full token , so it can present offline\nand does not disclose data to backend systems when presenting a VP\nHolder private key remains on device\nBackend does not keep the full VC , only references
                CoreApp->CoreApp: [DATA STORE] Store the full token (SD_JWT_VC + disclosures) in the on-device database
                note right of CoreApp #wheat:[DATA STORE] on-device database\ncredentialId , credentialType , vct\nissuer DID / issuer display name\nschemaId\nvalidFrom / validUntil\nstatus reference ( uri + idx )\ndisplay metadata
                CoreApp->CoreApp: [DATA STORE] Store credential metadata in on-device database
                CoreApp->CoreApp: Bind credentialId to holder key reference\nBind credentialId to deviceId
                CoreApp->CoreApp: Mark credential as available for presentation

            else Storage mode = CLOUD (encrypted on the device before upload)
                note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] Cloud credential model\nThe token is encrypted on the device , DW stores only ciphertext and metadata\nTo present a VP the app downloads the ciphertext , decrypts it on the device and signs with the on-device key\nPresenting needs a network connection\nHolder private key remains on device
                note right of CoreApp #wheat:[PENDING] Recovery of the data key when the device is lost or replaced\nWhether credential metadata on DW may be stored in clear
                CoreApp->CoreApp: Encrypt the full token (SD_JWT_VC + disclosures) on the device\nwith a data key protected by secure hardware (Secure Enclave / Android Keystore)
                CoreApp->DW: Store encrypted credential + Token | POST /dw/v1/credentials (DW endpoint 08)\n(credentialId , encrypted token , credential metadata)
                note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW cloud storage\nCitizenId , deviceId , credentialId\nencrypted token (DW cannot decrypt it)\ncredential metadata : credentialType , vct , issuer DID , validFrom / validUntil , status reference ( uri + idx )
                DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store encrypted credential in DW cloud storage
                CoreApp<--DW: 201 | cloud reference
                CoreApp->CoreApp: [DATA STORE] Store credential metadata + cloud reference in on-device database
                CoreApp->CoreApp: Bind credentialId to holder key reference\nBind credentialId to deviceId
                CoreApp->CoreApp: Mark credential as available for presentation

            end

            note over CoreApp #lightblue: 9.2 Secure Local Storage and Access Policy
            note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] Applies to the on-device database in both modes\nIn CLOUD mode it holds credential metadata and the cloud reference , not the full token
            note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] Target is OWASP MASVS-STORAGE level L2\nThe library provides only L1 , the gap must be implemented
            note right of CoreApp #wheat:[SPEC] Secure local storage\nAndroid : EncryptedSharedPreferences / Room encrypted DB\niOS : Keychain
            CoreApp->CoreApp: Use secure local storage for the on-device database (from 9.1)
            CoreApp->CoreApp: Encrypt the database with envelope encryption\nKEK in secure hardware protects DEK on disk , DEK encrypts the data files
            CoreApp->CoreApp: Set file protection so data is unreadable while the screen is locked\nnot only until first unlock after boot
            CoreApp->CoreApp: Protect credential access with device security\nbiometric / PIN / device unlock
            CoreApp->CoreApp: Store only the personal data that is necessary\ndo not keep readable claim copies without justification
            CoreApp->CoreApp: Prevent export of holder private key\nSecure Enclave / Android Keystore / StrongBox
            CoreApp->CoreApp: Configure usage policy\nrequire holder confirmation before presentation\nrequire holder signing before VP submission
CoreApp-->Mini: Credential stored | credentialId

            note over CoreApp,Engine #lightblue: 9.3 Wallet confirms receipt
            note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] Two ways are supported to send credential_accepted\n1. The app calls the notification endpoint directly (from App to VCVP Core , same path)\n2. The app reports to DW and DW sends the notification (used in this flow)\nWay 2 : the app passes notification_id , access token and notification_endpoint to DW\n(OpenID4VCI 1.0 section 11 : the Wallet MUST present a valid access token to the Notification Endpoint)\nDW acts as the server-side component of the Wallet (section 13.4)
            Mini->DW: Report issuance result + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/issuance_result (DW endpoint 06)\n(issuanceSessionId from response of 1.2 , result = ACCEPTED , notification_id , access token , notification_endpoint)
            DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ACCEPTED
            DW->Core: Notify credential_accepted with notification_id + access token | POST notification_endpoint (from issuer metadata , passed by the app) = /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification
            note right of Engine #wheat:[SPEC] The engine sets ACCEPTED when the credential is issued , not on notification\ncredential_accepted does not change state\ncredential_failure → ERROR | credential_deleted → REJECTED\nERROR and REJECTED set the Token Status List entry to INVALID , suspend , reactivate and revoke are refused afterwards (400 BR_0366)
            Core->Engine: Notify credential_accepted with notification_id + access token | POST /ssi/openid4vci/final-1.0/{credentialSchemaId}/notification (VCVP Core 19)\nevent = credential_accepted
            Engine-->Core: 204 (state stays ACCEPTED)
            Core->Core: [DATA STORE] Store wallet receipt in Documents table : WalletNotification (Event = credential_accepted , ReceivedAt)\n(document found by notification_id = EngineRefs[].RefNotificationId)
            Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of /ssi notification (event = credential_accepted , Correlation.DocumentId)
            DW<--Core: 204
            DW->DW: Prepare card/document data from applicant data (section 2)
            Mini<--DW: 200 (response of issuance_result) | digital card/document data
            Mini->CoreApp: Store card/document data (linked to credentialId)
            CoreApp->CoreApp: [DATA STORE] Store card/document data in on-device database\nlinked to the stored credentialId
            CoreApp-->Mini: Card/document data stored

            Mini-->User: Show digital card/document with a VC badge\n(card/document data from DW , linked to the stored verifiable credential)
        end

    end

else Holder rejects credential
    User->Mini: Reject
    Mini->DW: Reject offer + Token | POST /v1/virtualcards/offer_reject (DW endpoint 07)\n(issuanceSessionId from response of 1.2 , reason = HOLDER_REJECTED)
    DW->Core: Reject credential | POST /vcvp/v1/wallet/offers/reject (VCVP Core 20)
    Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) , caller channel = WALLET , ActorType = CITIZEN\nwrite access log
    Core->Core: Validate caller authorization
    alt Caller not authorized
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 20 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED , Correlation.DocumentId)
        DW<--Core: 403 | FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
        note over DW,Core #wheat: Reject not recorded in VCVP , the offer still expires by itself
    else Caller authorized

        note over Core #pink: 11. Handle Holder Reject
        Core->Core: Update status HOLDER_REJECTED\ndo not call engine , let the offer expire
        note right of Core #wheat:[AUDIT LOG] VCVPAuditLog\nEventType = DOCUMENT_OFFER_REJECTED\nActor (Channel = WALLET)\nReasonDetail\nCorrelation.DocumentId\nEventTime\nIntegrity.Hash , Integrity.PrevHash
        Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 20 (status = HOLDER_REJECTED , Correlation.DocumentId)

        DW<--Core: 200
    end
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = HOLDER_REJECTED
    Mini<--DW: Cancel issuance
    Mini-->User: Credential not issued , card/document not added
end


@enduml
